! Rhea the Moon Elf

*GM record — NPC of Freyja's authorship (noted to the record 2026-08-14). Register: Provisional-Synthesis; the Level 7 sheet remains unbuilt. Player-safe as written; her network's tradecraft stays at the table's discretion.*

!! The Shape of Her

''Level 7 · primary paths: Combat-Rogue / Artificer.'' She styles herself //Rhea the Moon Elf//; the family ledgers of ''Menzoberranzan'' would style her otherwise. A noble house's daughter driven into the deep dark and then to the surface — where the family //mad-maxxed around for a while// — until the Spider Queen's agents made them, and Rhea fled through the planar gates and found a way to Elyncia. The crossing rhymes with Telarus's own fall, and the two of them know it.

!! Tropes & Kit

* ''High-level drow magic'' — the old house's inheritance, carried far from the house.
* ''Steampunk prosthesis'' — the lost left arm and left leg rebuilt as enchanted magitech limbs: contraptions and weaponry built *into* them, a dungeon-crawler's toolkit worn as a body.
* ''Built to solo-crawl'' — in the manner the old tales give Robilar: traps expected, doors distrusted, retreat pre-planned.
* ''Blight-hardened'' — her magitech stands proofed against the rust-blight and against rust-monsters both; whatever her limbs are made of, the blight does not read it as food. *(Weld: the Named-iron / sky-iron / crucible-steel practices of the Curse of Iron canon — which proofing she uses stays hers to reveal.)*

!! Her Work in Elyncia

Since her arrival she has ''trained a cadre of agents'' and runs a ''small intelligence network for the Dragoness''. Rogues who don't make her cut go to the ''Adventurer's Guild'' — where they remain useful, and where, not coincidentally, her patroness's partner company gains a steady stream of vetted talent.

''For the last two months her network has sent back intel from the Neo-Thracian Nexus'' — the readings that shaped the Patroness's summit timing and the company's sub-mission both.

!! Hooks Held Open

* Whether any of her Neo-Thracian agents remain in place when the company lands.
* What the Spider Queen's agents made, exactly, and whether the making reached Elyncia behind her.
* The prosthetics' maker — self-built, commissioned, or inherited from someone who no longer needs them.

